# Demo5 Project

A simple demo project for learning, prototyping, and extending a small application with a clean structure.

## Overview

This repository, `narshru/demo5project`, is intended to serve as a starter project or demonstration codebase. It is organized to make it easy to understand the layout, run the app locally, and build on top of the existing structure.

## Features

- Simple, readable project layout
- Easy setup and local execution
- Suitable for demonstration, testing, and iteration
- Extensible foundation for additional modules or features

## Prerequisites

Before running the project, make sure you have the following installed:

- Git
- A supported runtime for the project (for example Node.js, Python, or another dependency required by the codebase)
- Package manager or environment tooling appropriate to the project stack

## Getting Started

1. Clone the repository:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/narshru/demo5project.git
   cd demo5project
   ```
2. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   npm install
   ```
   If the project uses another runtime or dependency manager, follow the package-specific setup steps instead.
3. Start the application:
   ```bash
   npm start
   ```
4. Open the app in your browser or the relevant local development environment.

## Project Structure

```text
demo5project/
├── src/             # Application source code
├── public/          # Static assets or frontend resources
├── tests/           # Test files
├── package.json     # Project configuration and scripts
├── README.md        # Project documentation
├── .gitignore       # Ignored files and directories
└── LICENSE          # Project license
```

## Development

Use the project’s existing scripts or build tools for day-to-day development:

```bash
npm run build
npm test
```

Customize the code and structure as needed for your own implementation or demo goals.

